<attribute name="sectionDescription" nodeId="de85c544">Guide the team in identifying what caused the sprint to be what it was by considering root causes. Review conditions,
interactions or patterns in the data gathered in the previous step. The team can employ a number of methods to perform this
diagnosis including a fish-bone diagram or 5-whys analysis. Regardless of the method, aim to obtain agreement among the
team as to the root causes and significant events that impacted their ability to perform work (either positively or
negatively) during the sprint. Steer the team away from generating solutions in this part of the meeting.</attribute>
